    {
      "id": "ctc89ip",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3.4.3 Punjab Police Sub-Inspector (SI) :Key Facts for Exam"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p18ru02",
      "content": "The Sub-Inspector (SI) is the Station House Officer (SHO) of a police station under normal circumstances. Key powers and duties:"
    },
    {
      "id": "zdaw1bx",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "An SI is a Gazetted Officer in Punjab Police.",
        "An SI can register FIR (First Information Report) under CrPC Section 154.",
        "An SI can conduct investigation and arrest without warrant for cognizable offences.",
        "An SI can grant bail in bailable offences under CrPC Section 436.",
        "The Punjab Police Recruitment Board conducts SI recruitment exams.",
        "Punjab Police Act 2007 governs the structure and powers of Punjab Police.",
        "SI (Detective) and SI (Executive) are separate cadres in Punjab Police."
      ]
    },
